{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>תבאמו.</b> Moses prophesied that he would not enter the land — therefore it does not say ״תְּבִיאֵנוּ״ (Bava Batra 119)." "<b>מכון לשבתך.</b> The Temple below is set corresponding to the Throne above, אֲשֶׁר פָּעַלְתָּ (Mekhilta)." "<b>מקדש ה'.</b> Its accent is a major zaqef, to separate it from the divine Name that follows it: הַמִּקְדָשׁ אֲשֶׁר כּוֹנְנוּ יָדֶיךָ ה׳. Beloved is the Temple — the world was created with one hand, as it says ״אַף יָדִי יָסְדָה אֶרֶץ״ (Isaiah 48), but the Temple with two hands. And when will it be built with two hands? In the time that ״ה׳ יִמְלֹךְ לְעֹלָם וָעֶד״ — in the time to come, when all sovereignty is His."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:32.583594649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}